across the channels that matter to the business.Video editing: Long-form and short-form editing, repurposing, color grading, motion graphics, captions and audio cleanup.YouTube channel operations: Metadata, thumbnails, publishing schedules, playlists and performance reporting.AI UGC creative: AI avatar videos, AI voiceover, product demo creative and image-to-video production.Explore Content CreationAI AutomationAI automation for business workflowsAutomation only helps when it is built around a process someone actually follows today. Innoventix Hub's automation pillar starts with mapping that process, then chooses the right tool for the job: a small business automation package for common sales and operations workflows, a custom CRM when off-the-shelf platforms cannot represent a business's pipeline, a GoHighLevel implementation when that platform's ecosystem fits, or an n8n build when the business needs custom logic connecting several existing tools.Small business automation: Marketing sequences, lead follow-up, pipeline management and reporting workflows.Custom CRM development: Bespoke CRM systems built around a specific pipeline, fields and reporting need.GoHighLevel implementation: Setup, migration, pipelines, calendars and workflow automation inside GHL.Explore AI AutomationAI Voice AgentsAI voice agents for business callsVoice AI has matured enough that a well-built agent can handle a real phone conversation: answering common questions, qualifying a lead, checking availability and booking an appointment, or explaining an order status, all without a caller feeling like they hit a dead-end menu. It has not matured to the point of replacing a human team for every call, and Innoventix Hub does not present it that way.Inbound call handling: Answering calls, understanding intent and routing to the right outcome.Lead qualification: Structured questions that capture the details a sales team needs.Appointment workflows: Checking availability and booking directly into a connected calendar.Explore AI Voice AgentsWeb DevelopmentWeb development for websites and business applicationsWeb development at Innoventix Hub is treated as a core discipline, not an outsourced afterthought bolted onto content or automation work. It covers three connected services: custom web application development for dashboards, portals and bespoke tools; WordPress development for marketing sites, blogs and WooCommerce stores; and web design and UX for the research and interface decisions that sit underneath both.Custom web applications: Dashboards, portals and bespoke tools built with modern frameworks.WordPress development: Custom themes, plugins, WooCommerce stores and site migrations.Web design and UX: User journeys, wireframes and interface design behind every build.Explore Web DevelopmentHow a project moves forward1DiscoverA strategy call to understand your goals, current setup and what a realistic scope looks like across content, automation, voice or web.2PlanA clear proposal covering deliverables, process, timeline factors and the specific team member leading the work.3BuildProduction, development or automation work carried out in reviewable stages with regular checkpoints for feedback.4RefineTesting, revisions and a handover that leaves you with documentation and a clear picture of what happens next.A small, specialist teamFive people, each responsible for a specific part of your project.URUbaid ur RehmanFounder & CEOATAtiqAutomation SpecialistHDHaiderContent Production LeadHSHussainUGC & Voice SpecialistUHUmer HashmiWeb Development LeadRead more about the teamGuides worth reading firstVideo Editing Brief Template for BrandsA clear brief is the single biggest factor in getting a video edit right on the first pass. This template walks through exactly what to include before you send footage to an editor.How to Repurpose Long Videos into ShortsOne long recording can produce several short clips if you know what to look for. Here is a repeatable process for turning a podcast, webinar or interview into short-form content.Video Editing Costs: What Changes the Quote?Video editing quotes vary widely because scope varies widely. This guide explains the specific factors that move a quote up or down, without inventing a fixed price list.YouTube Production Workflow: From Brief to PublishA consistent YouTube channel depends on a repeatable workflow, not just good individual videos. Here is the sequence of steps that keeps a channel publishing on schedule.Browse all resourcesFrequently asked questionsWhat does Innoventix Hub actually do?+Innoventix Hub combines four services: video and AI UGC content creation, AI automation and CRM work, AI voice agent development, and web development. Most clients start with one service and expand as needed.Do I need to use all four services?+No. Many clients work with Innoventix Hub on a single service, such as video editing or a WordPress rebuild. The four-pillar structure exists so that if your needs grow, one team already understands your business.How much does a project cost?+Cost depends entirely on scope. Each service page explains the specific factors that move a quote up or down, and a strategy call is the fastest way to get a scoped estimate for your own project.What happens on the free strategy call?+A conversation about your current goals and setup, followed by an honest recommendation on scope and next steps. There is no obligation to proceed afterward.Is your AI-generated content disclosed honestly?+Yes. AI UGC creative and voice agent interactions are never presented as a real customer or a real, unscripted person unless that is genuinely what they are.Ready to plan your next project?Book a free strategy call and walk through your goals, timeline and budget with the Innoventix Hub team. There is no obligation and no pressure, just a clear conversation about what is possible.Book Free Strategy CallContact the team
